  "raw": "en Español\n\n000\nABNT20 KNHC 210516\nTWOAT \n\nTropical Weather Outlook\nNWS National Hurricane Center Miami FL\n200 AM EDT Wed Oct 21 2026\n\nFor the North Atlantic...Caribbean Sea and the Gulf of America:\n\nOffshore of the East Coast of the United States (AL93):\nA storm-force non-tropical low pressure area located a few hundred \nmiles off the mid-Atlantic United States coast is producing some \nshower and thunderstorm activity primarily west and northwest of its \ncenter. Satellite imagery indicates that the low is still frontal. \nOver the next day or two, the low could gradually lose its frontal \nfeatures while it moves slowly north-northeastward over the Gulf \nStream, allowing the system to briefly develop subtropical \ncharacteristics. By the end of the week, the system is expected to \naccelerate northeastward away from the the eastern United States, \nand environmental conditions are expected to become unfavorable for \nadditional subtropical or tropical development. \n\nRegardless of the status of the system, high winds, coastal \nflooding, and dangerous surf are expected along portions of the U.S. \nEast Coast during the next few days. For more information, please \nconsult statements and warnings from local National Weather Service \noffices and the Weather Prediction Center, along with the High Seas \nForecasts and the Storm Warnings issued by the National Weather \nService.\n* Formation chance through 48 hours...medium...40 percent.\n* Formation chance through 7 days...medium...40 percent.\n\n&&\nHigh Seas Forecasts issued by the National Weather Service can be \nfound under AWIPS header NFDHSFAT1, WMO header FZNT01 KWBC, and \nonline at ocean.weather.gov/shtml/NFDHSFAT1.php\n\n$$\nForecaster Pierce/Pasch"
